  "body": "# OpenSpec 2.0\n\nOpenSpec now installs skills in `.agents/skills/` instead of keeping a separate copy for each coding agent. Tools that don't read this folder, like Claude Code and Kiro, get links to the same skills.\n\nWe're also removing the `/opsx:*` slash commands. Each command already has a matching skill, so there's no need to maintain both.\n\nThe OpenSpec workflows themselves haven't changed.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Skills are installed in `.agents/skills/`.** Every tool uses the same skills, without duplicate files across folders.\n- **`/opsx:*` commands are removed.** For example, `/opsx:propose` becomes `/openspec-propose` (or `$openspec-propose` in Codex). You can also just ask your agent for the work.\n- **`openspec update` removes files generated by older versions.** This includes old slash commands and duplicate skills. Files you've changed in the old locations are kept and listed.\n- The `delivery` setting is no longer needed. Existing configs keep working.\n- Amazon Q Developer support is removed because it can't load skills. We recommend Kiro instead.\n\n## How to upgrade\n\nUpdate the OpenSpec CLI, then run this in each project and commit the changes:\n\n```bash\nopenspec update\n```\n\nTo preview the changes first, run `openspec update --dry-run`.\n\n**Note:** if you edited OpenSpec's skills directly in `.agents/skills/`, `openspec update` overwrites those edits. Save them before upgrading.\n\nSee the [upgrade guide](https://openspec.dev/docs/upgrade-to-2) for more details.\n\n## Fixes\n\n- `openspec completion install` no longer edits PowerShell profiles when run from Windows cmd.exe.\n- `openspec instructions apply` no longer cuts off tasks that span several lines in `tasks.md`.\n\n**Full changelog:** [v1.17.0...v2.0.0](https://github.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec/compare/v1.17.0...v2.0.0)\n",
